  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "On 25 March 1948, some girls riding horses on the road to Hart Canyon, near Aztec, New Mexico, are said to have been turned back, around the time a flying saucer is claimed to have crashed there. A researcher named Scott Ramsey, who interviewed witnesses to the Aztec case, tells Michels that one of the women recalled it and that when he asked how she knew the date, she said, \"Cuz it was my birthday.\" If true, her memory would fix the date of the alleged crash and the cordon around it."
}
